et of Ministers of Turkmenistan.","image":"Serdar Berdimuhamedow (2022-06-10).jpg","birth":1981.7232876712328,"death":null},"Q57530":{"label":"Gurbanguly Berdimuhamedow","description":"Turkmen politician and president of Turkmenistan (2006–2022)","enwiki":"Gurbanguly Berdimuhamedow","summary":"Gurbanguly Mälikgulyýewiç Berdimuhamedow (born 29 June 1957) is a Turkmen politician, lawyer and former dentist who is the de facto leader of Turkmenistan, formally serving as chairman of the People's Council of Turkmenistan since 2021. He previously served as the second president of Turkmenistan from 2006 to 2022, when he entered into a power-sharing arrangement with his son, Serdar, the current president. \nA lawyer and former dentist, Berdimuhamedow served in the government of the president, Saparmurat Niyazov, as the minister of health in 1997 and as the deputy cabinet chair in 2001. He became acting president following Niyazow's death on 21 December 2006 and subsequently won the 2007 presidential election.","image":"Gurbanguly Berdimuhamedov on July 16, 2025.jpg","birth":1957.490410958904,"death":null},"Q82918":{"label":"Saparmyrat Nyýazow","description":"President of Turkmenistan from 1990 to 2006","enwiki":"Saparmurat Niyazov","summary":"Saparmurat Atayevich Niyazov (19 February 1940 – 21 December 2006) was a Turkmen politician and dictator who led Turkmenistan from 1985 until his death in 2006. He was the first secretary of the Communist Party of Turkmenistan from 1985 until 1991 and supported the 1991 Soviet coup attempt. He continued to rule Turkmenistan as the first president for 15 years after independence from the Soviet Union in 1991.\nTurkmen media referred to Niyazov using the title His Excellency Saparmyrat Türkmenbaşy, President of Turkmenistan and Chairman of the Cabinet of Ministers.","image":"Nyyazov in February 1998.jpg","birth":1940.1338797814208,"death":2006.9698630136986}},"media":{"Flag of Turkmenistan.svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Flag_of_Turkmenistan.svg/330px-Flag_of_Turkmenistan.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Turkmenistan.svg","author":null,"license":"Public domain"},"Emblem of Turkmenistan.svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Emblem_of_Turkmenistan.svg/330px-Emblem_of_Turkmenistan.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emblem_of_Turkmenistan.svg","author":"Inductiveload","license":"Public domain"},"Serdar Berdimuhamedow (2022-06-10).jpg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Serdar_Berdimuhamedow_%282022-06-10%29.jpg/330px-Serdar_Berdimuhamedow_%282022-06-10%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Serdar_Berdimuhamedow_(2022-06-10).jpg","author":"Presidential Executive Office of Russia","license":"CC BY 4.0"},"Gurbanguly Berdimuhamedov on July 16, 2025.jpg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Gurbanguly_Berdimuhamedov_on_July_16%2C_2025.jpg/330px-Gurbanguly_Berdimuhamedov_on_July_16%2C_2025.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gurbanguly_Berdimuhamedov_on_July_16,_2025.jpg","author":"Press Service of the President of the Republic of Azerbaijan","license":"CC BY 4.0"},"Nyyazov in February 1998.jpg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Nyyazov_in_February_1998.jpg/330px-Nyyazov_in_February_1998.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nyyazov_in_February_1998.jpg","author":"Danny Gys","license":"CC BY 4.0"}},"names":["TKM","TM","Turcmenistán","Turcomannia","Turcomenistao","Turco